          "prompt_tps": 3679.0469516468115,
          "response_text": "Quantizing an LLM from FP16 to INT4 reduces memory footprint by 75% (16-bit \u2192 4-bit per parameter), enabling larger models or efficient deployment on memory-constrained hardware. This compression also accelerates inference throughput, as lower-precision operations (INT4) are faster to compute than FP16, improving tokens-per-second rates, especially on hardware optimized for integer arithmetic. However, output quality may degrade slightly due to reduced numerical precision, though techniques like dynamic scaling or mixed-precision training can mitigate this. The trade-off balances speed and memory gains against minor accuracy losses, making INT4 suitable for latency-sensitive or resource-limited scenarios.",
